WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:03.230 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  Jason Aldean the Academy of Country  Music's reigning Entertainer of the Year  is back in Las Vegas this weekend hoping  to take home the honor for the 3rd  straight year what's it like for you to  be back here man you know I think  everybody's sort of tried to make this  you know this thing about me coming back  to Vegas kind of tried to make it a  little bigger than it was for me that  you know I've got a million great  memories in Vegas you know and one  horrible one it's been just over six  months since all Dean's performance at a  music festival was tragically cut short  when a gunman opened fire on the crowd  from the 32nd floor of the Mandalay Bay  Hotel well I love this town I mean I  love Las Vegas I love the city and you  know was looking forward to coming back  out here and and and I think this is the  right setting for me you know to be out  here with the country music family you  know my friends and people in the  country music world the shooting last  October was the country's deadliest mass  shooting 58 people were killed and  hundreds injured all Dean invited some  of those survivors to watch his  rehearsal Friday afternoon what were you  thinking about as you were performing  for them I think more than anything just  kind of glad to see him here I just  think we're everybody that was there you  know we're all kind of forever bonded  man so it's always cool to see those  people and sort of catch up because you  know people don't get it unless they're  you know they were actually there and so  I think it's therapeutic for everybody  just to sort of talk about it a little  bit the healing process began less than  a week after the shooting when all Dean  performed the Tom Petty song I won't  back down on Saturday Night Live  did you realize how cathartic that would  be for the whole country you know I  think we knew that us you know  performing on that show and if we did it  the right way would be a you know a big  thing for everybody I felt like that was  sort of a you know not only a healing  moment for me but it was also a chance  for me to sort of tell everybody else  like you know this is horrible and it's  you know but it's it's it's okay to  start the healing process and start to  pick up the pieces and move on  over the past 13 years Jason Aldean has  become one of country music's biggest  stars selling more than 10 million  albums his eighth rearview town was  released on Friday that album was  recorded before the horrific events here  but the title track is really  interesting it's about looking forward  and not looking back to be honest pretty  much the whole album was done maybe  other than four songs or something by  the time the shooting happened but for  me it's about you know putting things  that have sort of held you down you know  things have been a black cloud hanging  over you sort of putting that in the  past and looking down the road to some  better days for CBS this morning  Saturday vladimir duthiers las vegas

